orthant 1 language

- # `↯/s.146.1` — `Shrink.Error`
+ # `↯/s.146.1` — `Shrink.Error`

- Raised when a classpath cannot be shrunk to the closed world its entry points reach.
+ Se lanza cuando un classpath no puede reducirse al mundo cerrado que alcanzan sus puntos de entrada.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- Shrinking recompiles the classes of a classpath from their TASTy, without the members nothing
- reaches, and then follows the references of the bytecode which results to decide which other
- classes go with them. This error covers a closed world which would not be sound, and the
- shrinker terminating abnormally.
+ La reducción recompila las clases de un classpath a partir de su TASTy, sin los miembros que nada
+ alcanza, y después sigue las referencias del bytecode resultante para decidir qué otras clases van
+ con ellas. Este error abarca un mundo cerrado que no sería sólido y la terminación anómala del
+ reductor.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ### `↯/s.146.1.1` — `Unsound`
+ ### `↯/s.146.1.1` — `Unsound`

- **Example.** `[↯/s.146.1.1] the classpath could not be shrunk because a problem was found: example.Main refers to render()Ljava/lang/String; of example.Page, which was removed`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.146.1.1] the classpath could not be shrunk because a problem was found: example.Main refers to render()Ljava/lang/String; of example.Page, which was removed`

- Something which was kept refers to something which was not. The reason carries every such
- reference, as `problems`: each was found either in the compiler's trees, before any bytecode
- was generated, or in the bytecode afterwards. It also covers a unit which could not be
- recompiled and could not be pinned in its place, with the compiler's own errors as the
- problems.
+ Algo que se conservó hace referencia a algo que no se conservó. El motivo lleva cada una de esas
+ referencias, como `problems`: cada una se encontró o bien en los árboles del compilador, antes de
+ generar ningún bytecode, o bien en el bytecode después. También abarca una unidad que no pudo
+ recompilarse ni fijarse en su lugar, con los propios errores del compilador como problemas.

- **Resolution.** A reference which only reflection makes is not one the analysis can find: keep
- the class it reaches, with `Shrink`'s `keep` or `shrinkOptions.keep`. A reference the analysis
- should have found is a fault in it; pinning the unit which makes the reference, with `pin` or
- `shrinkOptions.pin`, copies that unit as it was, and keeps everything it refers to.
+ **Solución.** Una referencia que solo hace la reflexión no es una que el análisis pueda encontrar:
+ conserva la clase que alcanza, con el `keep` de `Shrink` o con `shrinkOptions.keep`. Una referencia
+ que el análisis debería haber encontrado es un fallo suyo; fijar la unidad que hace la referencia,
+ con `pin` o `shrinkOptions.pin`, copia esa unidad tal como estaba y conserva todo aquello a lo que
+ hace referencia.

- ### `↯/s.146.1.2` — `Failed`
+ ### `↯/s.146.1.2` — `Failed`

- **Example.** `[↯/s.146.1.2] the classpath could not be shrunk because the shrinker terminated abnormally`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.146.1.2] the classpath could not be shrunk because the shrinker terminated abnormally`

- The reason carries the stack trace.
+ El motivo lleva la traza de pila.

